undef;To;;I"accuracy_sec;T;I"Optional[String[1]];T;I"
undef;To;;I"compose_file_name;T;I"String[1];T;I"'compose.yml';To;;I"service_timeout;T;I"Integer[60];T;I"600;To;;I"extra_systemd_config;T;I"Hash[String, String];T;I"{};To;;I"registries;T;I"Podman_compose::Registries;T;I"{};T;I"podman_compose::cron;F:@docstringIC:YARD::Docstring"Renders a compose file, creates a oneshot systemd service and a
timer unit. The timer fires on the configured schedule, starts the
compose stack, waits for completion, then tears it down.

Two run modes are supported:
- **full stack** (default): `podman-compose up --abort-on-container-exit`
  followed by `podman-compose down`. Useful when the job needs
  sidecars (database, queue, etc.).
- **single service** (`run_service`): `podman-compose run --rm <svc>`.
  Lighter weight, ideal when only one container does the work.;T:@object0:@summary0:@hash_flagF:
