;"I"summary;F;#I"&Install method for podman-compose;T;0;$0;0;%[␀;&I"/@summary Install method for podman-compose;T;'0;M@°;IC;[␀;(@ú;)IC;[␀;(@ú;*IC;[␀;(@ú;+IC;,{;-IC;,{␀;.T;/IC;,{␀;.T;.T;0{␀;1[␀;2[[@ûi;3T;:#Podman_compose::Install_method;5;6;7;8; [␀;9{␀;IC;"␀;T; [o;!
;"I"summary;F;#I"&Install method for podman-compose;T;0;$0;@úo;!
;"I"api;F;#@[;0;$0;@ú;%[␀;&@©;'0;@ú;F;:@†;;i␀;<@L;=I"=puppet_data_type_aliases::Podman_compose::Install_method;Fo;K;o;L;I"types/recreate_strategy.pp;T;I"TPodman_compose::Recreate_strategy = Enum['rolling', 'force-recreate', 'down-up';T;i;o;;F;i␀;i;MI"1Enum['rolling', 'force-recreate', 'down-up'];T;I"&Podman_compose::Recreate_strategy;T;IC;"`* `rolling`        - `up -d --remove-orphans`. Least disruptive; relies on
                     podman-compose's own change detection. May NOT pick up
                     `.env` content changes delivered via `env_file:` and
                     will NOT re-create existing networks.
* `force-recreate` - `up -d --force-recreate --remove-orphans`. Re-creates
                     every container so new env values and changed service
                     network membership are applied cleanly. Does NOT
                     re-create existing network definitions (subnet/driver).
* `down-up`        - `down` then `up -d --remove-orphans`. Tears the project
                     down (including its networks) and brings it back up, so
                     network topology changes are applied too. Causes a brief
                     downtime of the whole project.;T;0;0;F; [o;!
